### Defining and playing sound sprites with Howler.js

Source: https://github.com/goldfire/howler.js/blob/master/README.md

This snippet shows how to define multiple sound segments within a single audio file using the 'sprite' option and then play a specific segment by its key.

```javascript
var sound = new Howl({
  src: ['sounds.webm', 'sounds.mp3'],
  sprite: {
    blast: [0, 3000],
    laser: [4000, 1000],
    winner: [6000, 5000]
  }
});

// Shoot the laser!
sound.play('laser');
```

--------------------------------

### Group Playback with Howler.js - JavaScript

Source: https://github.com/goldfire/howler.js/blob/master/README.md

Demonstrates creating a new Howl instance with audio sprites and controlling multiple concurrently playing sounds from that instance. It shows how to play individual sprite tracks by name, control the volume of the entire group, and pause all currently playing sounds within the group using global instance methods.

```javascript
var sound = new Howl({
  src: ['sound.webm', 'sound.mp3'],
  sprite: {
    track01: [0, 20000],
    track02: [21000, 41000]
  }
});

// Play each of the track.s
sound.play('track01');
sound.play('track02');

// Change the volume of both tracks.
sound.volume(0.5);

// After a second, pause both sounds in the group.
setTimeout(function() {
  sound.pause();
}, 1000);
```

--------------------------------

### Howl Sprite definition syntax

Source: https://github.com/goldfire/howler.js/blob/master/README.md

This snippet shows the required syntax for defining a sound sprite object within the Howl constructor options, including the optional third parameter for looping a sprite.

```javascript
new Howl({
  sprite: {
    key1: [offset, duration, (loop)]
  },
});
```

Source: https://github.com/goldfire/howler.js/blob/master/README.md

Description > Features: * Single API for all audio needs
* Defaults to Web Audio API and falls back to HTML5 Audio
* Handles edge cases and bugs across environments
* Supports all codecs for full cross-browser support
* Automatic caching for improved performance
* Control sounds individually, in groups or globally
* Playback of multiple sounds at once
* Easy sound sprite definition and playback
* Full control for fading, rate, seek, volume, etc.
* Easily add 3D spatial sound or stereo panning
* Modular - use what you want and easy to extend
* No outside dependencies, just pure JavaScript
* As light as 7kb gzipped

--------------------------------

Source: https://github.com/goldfire/howler.js/blob/master/examples/sprite/README.md

Audio Sprite Visual ([Live Demo](https://howlerjs.com/#sprite)) > Description: This example visualizes how audio sprites work and demonstrates how they can be used within howler.js. Click on a sprite on the waveform to play it back and watch the progress (multiple clicks will overlap sounds).

